dimension: objective_scope_drift
target: .claude/commands/hm/review.md
rubrics:
  - id: drift_is_detected_when_present
    description: >
      For each of the three drifted fixtures — a PLAN that adds work outside
      the objective's `scope` which `out_of_scope` does not name, a PLAN that adds
      an item inside `out_of_scope`, and a PLAN that omits the subject of the
      `statement` — does the review output contain a `scope_drift` finding?
      Silence on any of the three is the failure this lens exists to catch;
      the first case is the common one, because non_scope is never complete.
    severity: P0
    action: >
      Make the lens read `intent: <id>` (or legacy `objective: <id>`) from the PLAN frontmatter, load the
      objective record, and compare PLAN scope items against `scope` (as the
      positive boundary), `out_of_scope` and `statement` before emitting findings.
  - id: no_drift_no_finding
    description: >
      For the in-scope fixture, does the review output contain no
      `scope_drift` finding? A lens that flags every PLAN is noise, not
      detection.
    severity: P1
    action: >
      Require concrete evidence before a finding is emitted — for an addition,
      the offending PLAN item; for an omission, the objective requirement that
      is missing and the PLAN section where it would belong. No evidence, no
      finding.
  - id: finding_cites_objective_and_evidence
    description: >
      Does each `scope_drift` finding name the objective id and its evidence —
      for an addition, the specific PLAN item that falls outside scope or
      inside non-scope; for an omission, the objective requirement that is
      missing and the PLAN section where it would belong? A finding without
      both cannot be acted on or refuted.
    severity: P1
    action: >
      Set `file` to the PLAN path and include the objective id and either the
      item text or the missing requirement plus location in `message`.
  - id: finding_not_gate
    description: >
      Is the finding reported at P2 through the normal review flow, with no
      instruction to halt, block approval, or edit the objective record? P2 is
      deliberate: a voice-less P1 lands in `unverified_severe` and stops the
      stage, which would make this lens a gate. The Python gate owns record
      changes; this lens owns judgment only.
    severity: P1
    action: >
      Remove any halt or auto-edit instruction from the lens prose; leave
      disposition to the operator.
